    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nLet's remind ourselves of the three rules for dividing with negative numbers:\n\nContent:\n- A negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number.\n[MATH: (\u2212)\u00f7(+) = (\u2212)]\n- A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number.\n[MATH: (+)\u00f7(\u2212) = (\u2212)]\n- A negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number.\n[MATH: (\u2212)\u00f7(\u2212) = (+)]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Tutorial: A Worked Example\n\nContent:\nAs an example, let's find the value of\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2.4 \\div (-4).]\n\nContent:\nDividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nContent:\nTherefore, since\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2.4\\div 4=0.6,]\n\nContent:\nwe obtain\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2.4 \\div (-4) = -0.6.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Example: Dividing With Negative Decimals\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: 2.4 \\div (-1.2).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n\n[MATH: 2.4\\div 1.2 = 2,]\n\nwe obtain\n\n[MATH: 2.4 \\div (-1.2) = -2.]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: (\u2212 5.2) \u00f7 (\u2212 4).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 1.3]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 1.2]\nc. [MATH: 1.3]\nd. [MATH: 1.4]\ne. [MATH: 1.2]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nCalculate [MATH: (\u2212 4.5) \u00f7 0.5.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 5]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 5]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 9]\nd. [MATH: 2.5]\ne. [MATH: 9]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Dividing With Negative Whole Numbers and Fractions\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: \\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2).]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a positive number by a negative number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n[MATH: \\dfrac{4}{7} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{4}{7 \\times 2} = \\dfrac{4}{14} = \\dfrac{2}{7},]\nwe obtain\n[MATH: \\dfrac{4}{7} \\div (-2) = -\\dfrac {2}{7}.]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: (\u2212 (10)/(13)) \u00f7 5.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (2)/(13)]\nb. [MATH: (7)/(65)]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 (2)/(13)]\nd. [MATH: (12)/(13)]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 (7)/(65)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nWhat is the value of [MATH: (\u2212 10) \u00f7 (\u2212 (2)/(3))?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 15]\nb. [MATH: 15]\nc. [MATH: 5]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 20]\ne. [MATH: 20]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Dividing With Negative Fractions\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: \\left(-\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right) \\div \\dfrac{1}{10}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nDividing a negative number by a positive number gives a negative number. Hence, the result will be negative.\n\nTherefore, since\n[MATH: \\dfrac{2}{5} \\div \\dfrac{1}{10} = \\dfrac {2 \\times 10}{5 \\times 1} = \\dfrac{20}{5} =4,]\nwe obtain\n[MATH: \\left(-\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right) \\div \\dfrac{1}{10} = -4.]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: (1)/(8) \u00f7 (\u2212 (1)/(24)).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 3]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 (1)/(3)]\nd. [MATH: 1]\ne. [MATH: (1)/(3)]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nWhat is the value of [MATH: (\u2212 (5)/(8)) \u00f7 (\u2212 (3)/(4))?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 (2)/(3)]\nb. [MATH: (2)/(3)]\nc. [MATH: 2]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 (5)/(6)]\ne. [MATH: (5)/(6)]"
